  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Food assistance and logistics response to Tropical Cyclone Freddy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project seeks to provide immediate lifesaving food assistance to affected populations by providing commodities or cash-based transfers, mitigating the direct humanitarian crisis in the aftermath of Tropical Cyclone Freddy. WFP provides in-kind assistance to 145,500 people in the targeted districts for one month. WFP facilitates access for air transport of urgent transport of life-saving cargo and search and rescue efforts in locations not accessible by road or river. WFP will facilitate access to 25 mt within secondary and tertiary road networks. Mobile storage units will also support adequate storage facilities for relief items. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 145,500 people, including 30,992 women, 43,796 men, 70,713 children, and including 16,878 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
